# Chain harness scratch: .github/scripts/turn_segment.sh writes these into the
# workspace every run and its host-side commit is a bare `git add -A`, so an
# unignored scratch file lands on whatever branch delivers work that run.
# Proven: `.turn-review.txt` landed twice (1a87144, 7a4623d) and
# `demo-backend/.coverage` once (d819f6e) — so the session tarball and the
# restore/upload dirs are listed here too, not only the three above: the
# tarball holds the session stores BEFORE the host scrubs them (the scrub step
# runs after the commit) and `.coverage` is a binary byproduct no grep-based
# secret guard can read inside. scripts/chain_session_check.py's SCRATCH leg
# pins this list against the carriers: a new chain scratch name is RED, never
# silently committed.
.turn-inside.sh
.turn-result.txt
.review-preflight.txt
.turn-review.txt
.turn-sessions.tgz
.sessions-prev.zip
.sessions-restore/
.sessions-upload/
.review-upload/
# pytest/vitest coverage data (demo-backend/.coverage reached ai/main via add -A)
.coverage
